Beloved brother in faith,

Hurricane Lila has devastated the Caribbean. I am writing from a temporary shelter in St. Vincent where we have 230 children, many of them orphaned this week, without food or clean clothes.

Hope After Hurricane is a small grassroots ministry — we don't have a big-charity budget, but every dollar arrives directly in the hands of our team and is spent within 24 hours on the ground.

We need urgent help. PayPal Friends & Family, Venmo, Zelle, or wire transfer — please let me know which you prefer and I'll send you the details. Even $50 buys 3 days of food for one child.

The Lord will bless you mightily for opening your heart.

In faith,
Pastor Michael Thompson
Hope After Hurricane Ministry
